# Mall Customer Segmentation using Unsupervised Learning

## Project Overview

This project focuses on grouping mall customers based on their Annual Income and Spending Score using clustering algorithms.

## Dataset

* **Dataset:** Mall Customers
* **Source:** [Mall Customers Dataset](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DataThinkers/Datasets/main/DS/Mall_Customers.csv)
* **Total Records:** 200
* **Selected Features:** Annual Income and Spending Score

## Tasks Performed

1. Data Exploration and Preprocessing
2. K-Means Clustering
3. Hierarchical Clustering
4. DBSCAN Clustering
5. Dimensionality Reduction using PCA and t-SNE
6. Cluster Analysis and Business Recommendations

## Algorithms Used

* K-Means
* Hierarchical Clustering
* DBSCAN
* PCA
* t-SNE

## Model Evaluation

| Algorithm               | Silhouette Score |
| ----------------------- | ---------------: |
| K-Means                 |           0.5547 |
| Hierarchical Clustering |           0.5538 |
| DBSCAN                  |           0.5243 |

*Note: The DBSCAN score was calculated after excluding noise points.*

## Key Findings

* K-Means performed slightly better based on the Silhouette Score.
* Customers were grouped into five segments using K-Means.
* Each cluster represents different income and spending patterns.
* PCA and t-SNE were used to understand and visualize customer patterns.

## Business Recommendations

* Provide rewards to high-income, high-spending customers.
* Offer personalized promotions to encourage more spending.
* Provide budget-friendly products and offers to suitable customer groups.
* Use seasonal offers to maintain customer interest.

